* 8-transistor complementary log-antilog cell (Hebert AES 4055 Fig. 4; the 2180/2181 core)
*
* Each leg has one NPN and one PNP junction in series, so the control law is
*   Iout/Iin = exp((V(ecp)-V(ecn))/(2*VT))   ->  ~6.0 mV/dB at 27 C
* and NPN/PNP differences (IS, ideality) are common to both signal polarities.
* The lower/upper devices are cross-coupled so that RC1..RC4 cancel the
* signal-dependent drop in the parasitic base/emitter resistances:
*   ideal RCx = r'ex(primary) + r'ex(cross-coupled),  r'ex = RE + RB/(beta+1)
*
* Pins as BLACKMER4. Params: RC = all four correction resistors,
* AR2/AR4/AR6/AR8 = area ratio of each output-side device to its input-side partner.
.subckt BLACKMER8 in out ecp ecn sym IDLE=20u CC=22p GBW=10e6 RC=1m AR2=1 AR4=1 AR6=1 AR8=1
XOA 0 in top OPAMP_IDEAL GBW={GBW}
CC1 top in {CC}
* primary log (input side) and antilog (output side) devices
XQ1 in  ecn e1 QNCORE
XQ2 out sym e2 QNCORE AR={AR2}
XQ3 in  ecp e3 QPCORE
XQ4 out ecn e4 QPCORE AR={AR4}
* lower cross-coupled PNP pair
XQ5 c5 c6 e1 QPCORE
XQ6 c6 c5 e2 QPCORE AR={AR6}
RC1 c5 bot {RC}
RC2 c6 bot {RC}
* upper cross-coupled NPN pair
XQ7 c7 c8 e3 QNCORE
XQ8 c8 c7 e4 QNCORE AR={AR8}
RC3 c7 top {RC}
RC4 c8 top {RC}
* bias generator: ideal floating copy of a 2 NPN + 2 PNP replica stack at IDLE
EB  top bot rp 0 1
IR  0 rp {IDLE}
XR1 r1 r1 rp QPCORE
XR2 r1 r1 r2 QNCORE
XR3 r3 r3 r2 QPCORE
XR4 r3 r3 0  QNCORE
.ends BLACKMER8
